\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{The half-turn average in sector blocks}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{For the real [half-turn](fdip-000L), the operator in sector coordinates is #{P=\operatorname{diag}(I_2,-I_2)}. Write
##{R=\begin{pmatrix}A&B\\ C&D\end{pmatrix}.}
Conjugation by #{P} sends #{R} to #{\begin{pmatrix}A&-B\\ -C&D\end{pmatrix}}. The average of \ref{fdip-008X} is therefore
##{E(R)=\begin{pmatrix}A&0\\ 0&D\end{pmatrix}.}
The represented projectors #{E_\pm=2^{-1}(I\pm P)} recover the same operator as #{E_+RE_++E_-RE_-}. The commutant of #{P} is isomorphic to #{M_2(\mathbb R)\times M_2(\mathbb R)}, while the image of the group algebra is the smaller algebra of scalar blocks #{\operatorname{diag}(xI_2,yI_2)}. Both identifications are the calculations of \ref{fdip-003T}.}
